# --- Bulk intermediate art renders (added 2026-08-03) -------------------------------------------
# Two directories held 9.9 GB of generated contact sheets / mosaics between them, which had kept
# three concurrent Act 1 sessions' work uncommitted. Both are REGENERABLE from scripts/ and
# nothing at runtime loads either. Everything else under design/ IS committed -- including the
# locked anchors in design/art-refs/, the town and dungeon source art, the specs, and the
# owner-review contact sheets.
# Ignore the 8.3 GB of blueprint renders, but NOT act1-final-art-geometry-r26 (52 MB):
# scripts/runtime_baseline.py pins that runtime/manifest.json by SHA and package.json's
# test:act1-r26 runs test-final.mjs from it. Ignoring it would break the gate on a fresh clone.
# Git cannot re-include a path under an excluded DIRECTORY, so each level is excluded by
# contents (/*) and the next level re-included.
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/act1-final-art-geometry-r26/
# ...and NOT the five files runtime_baseline.py reads via ACT1_HIFI_RUNTIME (as opposed to the r26
# pack above). verify_act1_overlay byte-compares each of these against its dist twin, so a fresh
# clone hits FileNotFoundError before it can even fail the comparison. Same defect the r26
# re-inclusion fixed, one directory up. hero-g3/ is laddered rather than re-included whole: the
# gate wants one 128 kB sprite sheet out of a 19 MB folder of evidence and reference renders.
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/index.html
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/walkable-polygons.js
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/walkable-route-state.js
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/path-corridor.js
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/hero-g3/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/hero-g3/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/act-by-act/act1/runtime-v2/hero-g3/hero-act1-female-walk-8x3-64-g3.png
# The COASTLINE. Act 1's painted terrain carries no water at all -- the sea is applied from this
# 128 kB boolean mask -- so scripts/act1_owner_paint_plate.mjs cannot build the collision plate
# without it and npm run test:map-engine fails at export_act1_runtime_override.mjs --check.
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/continent/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/continent/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/continent/continent-macro-g3/
design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/continent/continent-macro-g3/*
!design/review/overworld-art-blueprint/continent/continent-macro-g3/land-mask.npy
# The OWNER'S PAINTED TERRAIN -- the authority for Act 1's collision AND its art (owner, 2026-08-02:
# "please redo the collision setting based on what i created (my paint)"). The directory is 1.6 GB
# of art-tiles intermediates, so ignore the bulk and keep the three inputs: owner-terrain.json is
# what the collision plate is generated from, raw-export.json is its pristine pre-edit twin, and
# act1-smoothed-semantic.png is the mask render_material_map.py paints the terrain through.
# ~320 kB in total. Do not blanket-ignore this directory again; the repo cannot rebuild Act 1
# without these, and they are the one artefact here that is genuinely unregenerable.
design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/*
!design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/owner-terrain.json
!design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/owner-terrain.raw-export.json
!design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/art-tiles/
design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/art-tiles/*
!design/continent-terrain-class-method/owner-terrain/art-tiles/act1-smoothed-semantic.png
scripts/__pycache__/

# xcodebuild derived data from scripts/run-ios.sh
.ios-build/
